WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
[Shortwave static & carrier acquisition]

2
00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.250
This is GOR-9. This is GOR-9.

3
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.200
[Harmonic crystal signal-lock chime]

4
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:11.232
Galactic Outpost Radio, broadcasting from the High Basalt Shelf
on Asteroid 3-5-1 in Sector 9.

5
00:00:11.272 --> 00:00:16.930
Fourteen-two-eighty-five kilohertz upper sideband.
Zero-four-hundred Galactic Coordinated.

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.703
Space Weather, with emphasis on Sector 9.

7
00:00:20.743 --> 00:00:24.734
Coreward lanes are calm—solar flux one-seventy-four, K-index two.

8
00:00:24.774 --> 00:00:30.378
Locally, an electrostatic dust squall on the Meridian Plateau
has engulfed Relay KZ9-Omega.

9
00:00:30.418 --> 00:00:38.069
Sixty-kilovolt triboelectric arcing across the feedhorn is causing
minor phase-wobble in the number-four marzelvane bushing.

10
00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:40.240
Expect SINPO two-three-two-two-two.

11
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.617
Outpost Economics.

12
00:00:42.657 --> 00:00:48.711
Grade-B Deuterium pellets rose four percent today following
a dragline cable slowdown at Silicate Quarry 44-K.

13
00:00:48.751 --> 00:00:55.691
Outpost Nine will step Reactor Two down to twelve kilowatts after midnight;
Dormitory B should plug in auxiliary foot-warmers.

14
00:00:55.731 --> 00:01:04.500
Meanwhile, our monthly supply tender remains impounded at Quarantine Buoy Twelve
after customs misfiled replacement oscillator tubes as fermented brine tubers.

15
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:09.978
On the Hauser Correlator: Titan-Minor, three-eight-ninety kilohertz.

16
00:01:10.018 --> 00:01:13.150
Hydrographic Buoy N-24 reciting methane tide tables,

17
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.690
[3,890 kHz CW telemetry & metallic buoy bell clank]

18
00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:20.110
while migratory silt-striders rub against the guy-wires,
detuning the whip antenna.

19
00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:25.980
Callisto Dome Four, eleven-four-ten kilohertz.
Unlicensed noodle-market broadcaster Radio Corrugated,

20
00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.480
[11,410 kHz AM night-market lute & dipole blowtorch spike]

21
00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.620
peaking right as their engineer hit the dipole with a blowtorch.

22
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.602
And Intergalactic, M-Thirty-Three: a seven-hundred-year-old drift-buoy

23
00:01:36.642 --> 00:01:42.250
still issuing small-craft warnings for an ammonia sea
that evaporated in the Ming Dynasty.

24
00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:50.764
Finally, a late-night alert on the Euclid Signal Detector,
which scans the noise floor for signs of geometric intelligence.

25
00:01:50.804 --> 00:01:58.246
At zero-three-twelve UTC, inside unmanned Brine Evaporation Vat Nineteen
on Callisto-South, the detector locked onto Frame Seven:

26
00:01:58.286 --> 00:02:01.030
an unsuspecting parallelogram in the salt crust.

27
00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:07.362
Opposite sides parallel to two ten-thousandths of an arcsecond—
A-B to C-D, A-C to B-D—

28
00:02:07.402 --> 00:02:12.810
and somebody drew the diameter B-C,
bisecting the sludge into two congruent triangles.

29
00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:18.556
The Water Board claims a motorized mud-rake
lost a cotter pin and dragged sideways.

30
00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:20.870
It's always a broken cotter pin, folks.

31
00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:29.080
On the next broadcast: an unlicensed numbers station in the Trojans
reciting dumpling recipes in base-eight,

32
00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.947
and a suspected rhombus aboard an ice-hauler.

33
00:02:31.987 --> 00:02:37.680
From Asteroid 3-5-1 in Sector 9, this is GOR-9—
your eye to the cosmos, ear to the vacuum.

34
00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:38.770
[Harmonic crystal sign-off chime]

35
00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:39.120
[Carrier transitions to O.R.S. 351 orbital downlink]

36
00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:45.238
Remember, a like indication on your listening apparatus
gives us three kilowatts,

37
00:02:45.278 --> 00:02:50.480
and a subscription gets us one step closer
to upgrading our marzelvane emitters.

38
00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:58.620
[Soft Lydian harmonic chime & orbital carrier]
